// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// DEPENDS ON THE PREVIOUS TWO BUNDLES ALREADY BEING APPLIED, IN ORDER:
//   1. midnote-format-fix-and-features.tar.gz (the underline/strikethrough
//      toggle fix + contenteditable NoteContent + settings + colors)
//   2. midnote-schema-corrections.tar.gz (the .mdix schema fixes)
// This bundle's new/changed files call stripHtml()/htmlToPlainText() from
// richText.ts and assume NoteContent is already the contenteditable
// version — both only exist because of bundle 1. If those two haven't
// landed yet, apply them first (in that order), then this one. Not
// re-bundling their files here on purpose — same files, re-shipped a
// third time, would just be noise, and re-applying them (--file-strategy
// overwrite) is a harmless no-op once they're already there anyway.
//
// Multi-select: long-press a note/todo card to enter selection mode
// (haptic feedback where the WebView supports it), tap any card to
// toggle it, bottom action bar for Delete (confirmed)/Send/Merge/Export.
//
// A few things worth flagging plainly rather than letting them sit
// implicit in the code:
//
// - Merge is same-type only (notes with notes, todos with todos), per
//   the discussion on why: combining a todo's steps into a note's prose
//   doesn't have an obvious "right" behavior. It's also NOT calling
//   DixScript's real MdixMerger — checked that API directly
//   (with_strategy/with_array_strategy) before writing this, and it
//   merges *structured* fields across .mdix documents (scalars via
//   priority, arrays via concat+dedup), not prose. The app's entries
//   don't go through DixScript at runtime at all yet anyway (still
//   localStorage), so there's no live engine to hand this to regardless.
//   What's here is hand-written TypeScript; the tag/category merging
//   deliberately mirrors concat_dedup's actual behavior (union, no
//   duplicates) since that part of the idea does genuinely carry over.
// - A real, caught-before-shipping bug: merged todos regenerate fresh
//   ids for every merged step/annotation rather than keeping the
//   originals — two source todos can each independently have a step
//   "s1", and blindly concatenating would silently collide. Verified
//   this matters and that the fix works via an actual merge + zip
//   round-trip test (build → zip → unzip → compare), not just review.
// - A real gesture bug caught the same way, in longPress.ts: the first
//   version fired the tap handler after a big scroll-drag over a card,
//   which would have meant scrolling the list could accidentally
//   navigate into whatever note was under the finger when it lifted.
//   Simulated the exact pointerdown → 150px move → pointerup sequence,
//   confirmed it actually happened, then fixed it (a `moved` flag now
//   suppresses tap the same way it already suppressed long-press) and
//   re-confirmed with the same simulation plus the original tap/long-
//   press cases, so the fix didn't just trade one bug for another.
// - Send/Share uses the real (non-deprecated) Web Share API, not a stub —
//   also quietly fixed the single-note editor's own "Share" button while
//   touching this, since it was still a "coming soon" placeholder before
//   this. Same honest caveat as execCommand had: this can't be verified
//   in this sandbox at all, and specifically whether *file* sharing
//   (not just text) is supported depends on this Android WebView build,
//   not just the API's existence. Feature-detected with a text-only
//   fallback, then a download-instead fallback if navigator.share isn't
//   there at all — layered, not assumed to just work.
// - Export added a new dependency, fflate (~8kb, zero deps, pure JS —
//   picked over hand-rolling the ZIP binary format under time pressure,
//   given everything else already in flight this session). package.json
//   and package-lock.json are both in this bundle for that reason — sit
//   flat at the archive's own top level with explicit overrides:: below,
//   same pattern (and same reason) as the very first replacements bundle
//   this project shipped.
//
// Every other file sits nested under src/ at its real path — no
// dot-directories in this batch, so plain nested resolution applies to
// all of them, no overrides:: needed beyond the two root files.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "Mid-D-Man"
  features   -> "data,quickfuncs"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~target<object>(name, path) { return { name = name, path = path } }
)

@DATA(
  target_root = "."

  overrides::
    target("package.json", "package.json")
    target("package-lock.json", "package-lock.json")
)
